// The BOOTSTRAP FIXTURE CORPUS — a small, frozen, hand-picked set of library artifacts.
//
// ADR-0302 D1 makes the live Cloud SQL store the only source of truth and decommits
// `apps/studio/data/knowledge.json`. But ADR-0302 D3 deliberately keeps `STORYTREE_DB_USER` OUT of
// `pnpm -r test` (it is set per-step in ci.yml, never at job level) so the unit suites stay
// HERMETIC. Those two rules together mean the suites cannot follow the generators onto the live
// store — they need a corpus that needs no credential.
//
// This is that corpus, and the three properties that make it safe are all deliberate:
//
//   SMALL     — 22 artifacts, one per shape a suite actually names, rather than a mirror of the
//               219-unit seed it replaces. Nothing here is load-bearing for production.
//   FROZEN    — it is NOT regenerated from live and NOT reconciled against it. Drift is the intended
//               state, not a defect: a fixture that tracked live would re-create exactly the
//               seed↔live coupling ADR-0302 D4 deleted the machinery for. Nothing here is a claim
//               about what the Library currently says.
//   CLOSED    — every `asset:` ref resolves WITHIN this set (dangling ones were dropped on
//               extraction), so nothing here needs a transitive closure maintained behind it.
//
// It is TYPED and inline rather than a JSON file on disk on purpose: no path resolution, no
// `STORYTREE_REPO_ROOT`, no repo-root derivation — so it works from a worktree, a foreign checkout,
// or a bundle, which is precisely where the departing seed's `dataPath()` was fragile.
//
// WHAT DEPENDS ON WHICH ENTRY, because a "tidy the fixture" pass would otherwise break suites in
// another package: `edit-first-curation` and `pull-based-context-architecture` are named by id in
// the CLI's dashboard/doctrine assertions; `glossary-wins` carries the `doc:` refs the tree-focus
// OUTBOUND test needs; `trunk` → `approval-gated-trunk` is the INBOUND back-edge pair;
// `live-store-is-the-edit-surface` is the doctrine pointer a write-without---pg refusal prints;
// `merge-ceremony` is kept for its genuinely multi-KB `steps` field (the `--raw` byte-exactness
// test) and its real `surfaces` prose; `deep-modules` is what the studio UAT searches for. The two
// `adr` rows are the studio UAT's DECISION tier (ADR-0425 dec 4): its walkthrough opens a decision
// through the Library lens, moves from `adr-0002` to `adr-0013` through the finder, and reaches
// `adr-0002` as the decision behind `deep-modules`. Nothing LINKS them: the citation pointers that
// once did went with the `references` field (`fa4f96a5`), and the journey moved with that removal
// rather than growing edges to keep a leg alive (ADR-0605; the rows carry no `dependsOn` on
// purpose — ADR-0477 D6 fences which artifacts get one). They are here because
// ADR-0403 dec 1 made decisions ordinary artifacts and deleted `docs/decisions/`, so the offline
// sandbox had NO decision to open at all and that leg of the journey had no subject. Their bodies
// are deliberately abridged: this is a sandbox seed, not an archive. The four
// AGENTS are here because `drive` RENDERS them into prompts and its suites must do so without a
// credential: `session-orchestrator` (orchestrate / chat-stream), `red-builder` + `green-builder`
// (the leaf's per-phase system prompts, ADR-0051 §4) and `librarian-curator` (the post-build
// curation prompt). Their own prose is verbatim; only their ref LISTS are trimmed. `plan` and
// `anchor-implementation-surface` are the two ids `context-traversal-capture`'s UAT suite reads by
// SPAWNING the real CLI against a fixture door — it asserts on the recorded visit's `nodeId`, so the
// ids are load-bearing there even though nothing asserts their content.
//
// Consumers: the hermetic suites in `packages/cli`, `packages/drive` and `packages/library`, and
// the studio's `STORYTREE_STUDIO_STORE=json` offline sandbox. Anything that must report on the REAL
// corpus reads the LIVE store instead (`openCorpusStore`, ADR-0307 D4) — a check rung may hold a
// connection; a hermetic test may not.
//
// GENERATED ONCE from the seed at the moment it was deleted, then committed as source. There is no
// regeneration script and there should not be one: the next edit here is a hand edit.

